From 8a4e07260ad7e4a388754ec0d92ddc7816e5c94d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 10:22:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(facts): activate in-process board and project-tree
 owners [daveey]

Why: published canonical consumers were inert without a trusted serving owner.
Legacy board/tree requests still hydrated source state despite the facts API.

Own native detached board/shadow/catalog and project-tree captures through the
existing ContentOwner feed, in-process ctx.facts.v1 transport and pure canonical
reducers. Bind board cutover at the trusted bundled-plugin mount and tree at the
outer app lifespan, retaining links and plugin lifetime ordering. Keep native
host adapters outside the plugin boundary and pass existing plugin serializers
explicitly through the trusted mount.

HERMES_FACTS_BOARD is read only at startup, defaults ON, and OFF restores the
legacy board lifetime once while leaving tree activation absent. Cold, missing,
foreign-scope and failed captures return retryable unavailability, not legacy
hydration. Failed shutdown blocks admission while retaining retryable custody;
healthy sibling resources still drain. Current-board selection uses the captured
catalog, never request-time discovery. Authorized board/profile rosters are
startup-bound; new scopes fail closed until a subsequent authorized boot.

Proof:
- Original nine-suite baseline: 52 passed (raw inventory-baseline.log).
- Broad canonical board/tree/native/startup suite: 306 passed in 38 files.
- Boundary lint, unittest safety and handler ledger: 18 passed in 3 files.
- Actual startup/current-selector/direct+HTTP entry tests: green.
- Adjacent caller gate: green (raw caller-gate.log).
- Full scripts/check --base origin/main: exit 0 after boundary extraction.
- RED/GREEN actual mount and app-lifespan entry tests, capture/project parity,
  stale recovery, source vectors, selector/byte bounds, native mutations,
  request legacy/source tripwires, OFF rollback and failed-drain retry controls.

Evidence boundaries: local native hints plus <=30s recapture and 60s local
validity do not imply <1s upstream truth. No dedicated fact host; no sessions
sidebar/stamps ownership changes. Required CI, independent exact-head review,
canonical shipping and naturally routed live boot/mutation/rollback proof are
separate gates; no live activation or performance claim is made by these tests.
